\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Evaluation of pose sequence costs via pose interpolation {\color  {darkgreen}\begin  {CJK*}{UTF8}{gkai}\relax \fontsize  {9}{10pt}\selectfont  in various grasp candidates\end  {CJK*}}. (a) Interpolated object motion from Goal to Start ($\mathbf  {T}_{\mathrm  {mid}}$). (b) Comparison of energy landscapes: (i) Naive summation $J^{+}_{s}$ exhibits spurious minima due to asymmetric connectivity; (ii) Truncated objective $J^{h}_{s}$ suffers from flat surfaces (vanishing gradients); (iii) Proposed cost $J_{s}$ ($\lambda _{\mathrm  {reg}}=0.5$) shows a distinct global minimum with strong gradients. (c) Ground truth count of shared grasps, confirming that $J_{s}$ correctly identifies the valid regrasp region.{\color  {darkgreen}\begin  {CJK*}{UTF8}{gkai}\relax \fontsize  {9}{10pt}\selectfont  where $|\mathcal  {G}_{\mathrm  {shared}}|$ denotes the number of shared grasps for individual pose pairs ($(\mathbf  {T}_{\mathrm  {init}}, \mathbf  {T}_{\mathrm  {mid}})$ or $(\mathbf  {T}_{\mathrm  {mid}}, \mathbf  {T}_{\mathrm  {goal}})$). Furthermore, $|\mathcal  {G}_{\mathrm  {shared}}|_s$ represents the sum of shared grasps across the entire sequence $(\mathbf  {T}_{\mathrm  {init}}, \mathbf  {T}_{\mathrm  {mid}}, \mathbf  {T}_{\mathrm  {goal}})$, counted only when both transitions are simultaneously feasible.\end  {CJK*}}}}{5}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig_shared_grasp_seq_exp}{{5}{5}{Evaluation of pose sequence costs via pose interpolation \lqin {in various grasp candidates}. (a) Interpolated object motion from Goal to Start ($\mathbf {T}_{\mathrm {mid}}$). (b) Comparison of energy landscapes: (i) Naive summation $J^{+}_{s}$ exhibits spurious minima due to asymmetric connectivity; (ii) Truncated objective $J^{h}_{s}$ suffers from flat surfaces (vanishing gradients); (iii) Proposed cost $J_{s}$ ($\lambda _{\mathrm {reg}}=0.5$) shows a distinct global minimum with strong gradients. (c) Ground truth count of shared grasps, confirming that $J_{s}$ correctly identifies the valid regrasp region.\lqin {where $|\mathcal {G}_{\mathrm {shared}}|$ denotes the number of shared grasps for individual pose pairs ($(\mathbf {T}_{\mathrm {init}}, \mathbf {T}_{\mathrm {mid}})$ or $(\mathbf {T}_{\mathrm {mid}}, \mathbf {T}_{\mathrm {goal}})$). Furthermore, $|\mathcal {G}_{\mathrm {shared}}|_s$ represents the sum of shared grasps across the entire sequence $(\mathbf {T}_{\mathrm {init}}, \mathbf {T}_{\mathrm {mid}}, \mathbf {T}_{\mathrm {goal}})$, counted only when both transitions are simultaneously feasible.}}{figure.5}{}}
